{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed by direct reproduction against process_status on b97d414b8e2: after open->closed with all 4 close keys then closed->open, the reduced state still held force_close_reason/close_class/close_reason/completion_expectation; a following clean open->closed kept force_close_reason='bypass'. _fold_close_metadata only writes (present-only, gated on status=='closed'), and no step cleared them on leaving closed. Comparison: _clear_claimed_session already clears claim provenance on the winning in_progress exit.\n\nFix: new _clear_close_metadata (guard current_status=='closed' and status!='closed') called at both winner sites only; _fold_close_metadata unchanged. _REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION 7->8 so stale caches recompute. New tests/unit/test_reducer_status.py: 4 of 6 tests failed before the fix (reopen clears, clean re-close, end-to-end library force/reopen/close with forced STATUS event still in the log, v7 stale cache); the 2 fork tests (losing reopen keeps winner metadata, losing close does not overwrite) passed before and after. 64 tests across the new file, test_administrative_close_dispositions, test_processors_status_split, test_updated_at pass.\n\nOut of scope, filed as sugarcandy-fusible-hogget: SNAPSHOT compiled_state carrying stale keys (8 closed + 4 open/in_progress SNAPSHOTs in this tracker)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792362446929412447,"uuid":"561d1b7d-1e3a-464a-b968-c1bf0cf19be7"}